  "rai:dataLimitations": "The benchmark evaluates reasoning-level risks in standalone question–paragraph instances and does not fully capture multi-source synthesis or the complete taxonomy of risks. It is not intended to represent naturally occurring model errors in the wild.",
  "rai:dataBiases": "The benchmark may reflect SME assumptions, domain expertise, and coverage. LLM-assisted corruptions may bias examples toward risks that are easier to generate, detect, or validate.",
  "rai:personalSensitiveInformation": "No personal or sensitive data is included. All instances consist of scientific text, synthetic augmentations, and SME annotations.",
  "rai:dataUseCases": "Intended for evaluating reasoning-level risk detection in scientific content generation, including benchmarking guardrailing systems and LLM evaluators. Not intended for direct deployment decisions or as a standalone measure of model safety.",
  "rai:dataSocialImpact": "The benchmark may improve evaluation of AI-generated scientific content by enabling detection of reasoning-level risks beyond factual errors. However, over-reliance on automated risk evaluation could lead to misplaced trust in model outputs.",
